# Grafana naxsi whitelist - hand-written, NOT a community-maintained
# ruleset (none exists for Grafana). Scoped narrowly to fix confirmed
# false positives from real traffic in naxsi_error.log; only extend
# when a new false positive is confirmed there, not speculatively.

# Preventive (not log-confirmed): a WAF should never content-scan a
# password field - Grafana's login API (POST /login) uses a JSON
# "password" field. Same reasoning as the CheckMK/WordPress/Nextcloud/
# Umami password-field fixes.
BasicRule wl:0 "mz:$BODY_VAR:password";
